Design: ~/dev/io-k8s-p5/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-crd-design.md (D11-D17). Plan: to be written once IO::K8s steps 3 and 5 have landed.

- Aggregated discovery (GET /apis, Accept application/json;g=apidiscovery.k8s.io;v=v2;as=APIGroupDiscoveryList, per-group fallback) replaces /openapi/v2 as the source of the cluster resource map: groups, versions, plural, Kind, scope, preferred version. Cached per instance, invalidated by ensure_crd. /openapi/v2 becomes lazy (AutoGen only).
- Kubernetes::REST->new(with => [...]) mirrors IO::K8s; the fetched spec is passed as openapi_spec. The cluster map stops inventing IO::K8s::Api::<Group> names for groups the distribution does not ship (today: cilium.io -> nonexistent class, cert-manager.io -> invalid package name).
- Resolution order: +Class, providers, AutoGen (spec loaded), IO::K8s::Unstructured when discovery confirms the GVK (default on here), else the fail-closed error. Bare Kind resolves to the group's preferred version.
- ensure_crd(@classes): ensure of each class's to_crd, wait for Established with timeout, invalidate discovery.
- bin/kube_crd2class -f file.yaml | --from-cluster Kind: CLI over IO::K8s's emitter API.
- Finish ticket 22 (minikube runner) as the test bed; kubernetes-ocp then replaces register_resource_providers with with => [...].
Depends on: io-k8s-p5 k94, k96.

